What jitterKindT Is

Docket item 3 (2026-10-20), R0: the two shapes generateParse builds CodE from, each in a body the jitter compiles,
read back at top level (interpreted, so the reading is the same instrument in both runs). Born red on trunk 6f360e3.
The interpreted twin is this file with the `jitter;` line deleted (genLadder/pop.sh does it).

  JK-1  jkFill prints the literal "abc" into jkBuf. Read back: twin abc, jitted 3 -- jitPrintList emits the literal
        as an i32 load (its count, the length) because it decided the part's kind at build.
  JK-2  jkCopy assigns jkBufI (filled at top level, interpreted, with xyz) to jkX. Twin xyz, jitted a number that
        changes run to run -- jitEmitAssign stores an i32 load of the buffer. The row pins its SHAPE (all digits),
        never its value: an address-like number is H3 noise.
  JK-I  jkBufI read back after the copy: xyz on both roads -- the source is untouched, so JK-2's fault is the copy.
